I sit down at Peter's desk.
We look at his large screen.
Peter is also a software engineer.
He is a good colleague, and we write a lot of code together.
Today he looks very tired.
"What are you doing, Peter?" I ask.
"I have a big problem," he answers.
"I have worked on this error for three hours."
I smile and look closely at the code.
We often solve complex problems together in our work.
Suddenly I see something strange on the screen.
It is a very small mistake.
"Try to look here," I say and point at the screen.
"You have written a wrong word here."
Peter looks quietly at the screen for two seconds.
Then he laughs loudly.
"You are absolutely right," Peter says.
"I have worked for three hours, and then it is just one small error!"
I laugh too, because all software engineers know that situation.
We fix the error, and the program finally works perfectly.
